sqrt{1+\\theta}^2))+3\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt{1-\\theta + 9}}}{1+\\theta)^2 1}{9(1 + \\theta)(1 - \\theta)} = \\frac{9}{5(1+\\theta)(1-\\theta)} = \\frac{9}{5(2-\\theta)}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the numerator becomes \\(5f(1) = 5 \\cdot \\frac{9}{5(2 - \\theta)}\\), and the final answer is \\(\\frac{5 \\times 9}{5(2 - 1)}\\). So:\n\n\\[\nf(1) = \\frac{5 \\times 9}{5(2\\sqrt{2} + 1)} = \\frac{9}{4\\sqrt{2} + 4} = \\frac{9(4\\sqrt{2} - 4)}{(4\\sqrt{2} + 4)(4\\sqrt{2} - 4)} = \\frac{9(4\\sqrt{2} - 4)}{32}.\n\\]\n\nThus, simplifying, \\(f(1) \\approx 9\\left(\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2} + 4}\\right)\\). Finally, we get the integer value of \\(f(1)\\) by rationalizing the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{9 \\left(\\frac{4\\sqrt{2} - 4}{4}\\right) = 2 \\sqrt{2} - 4 \\approx 2(3 \\times 3 \\times 2)- 4=7= 3}.\n\\]",
